Feature: Tempo training
  As a musician using the metronome TUI
  I want the tempo to automatically increase every N measures
  So that I can train up to faster tempos without manually bumping BPM

  Background:
    Given the metronome app has started

  @ft:12
  Scenario: Enable tempo training
    Given the metronome is playing
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training line should read "Tempo Training: on"

  @ft:13
  Scenario: Disable tempo training
    Given tempo training is enabled
    When  I press "t"
    Then  the tempo training line should read "Tempo Training: off"

  @ft:14
  Scenario: Tempo training increases BPM after the configured number of measures
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"

  @ft:15
  Scenario: Tempo training stops increasing at the target BPM
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures and a target of 130
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    When  8 more measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 130 BPM"
    And   the tempo training line should read "Tempo Training: target reached (130 bpm)"

  @ft:16
  Scenario: Tempo training does not advance while stopped
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is stopped
    When  8 measures worth of time elapses
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"

  @ft:17
  Scenario: Default tempo-training step size
    Then  the tempo training line should read "Tempo Training: off, step 10 bpm / 8 measures"

  @ft:18
  Scenario: Increase the tempo-training step size
    Given the tempo-training step is 2 BPM
    When  I press "]"
    Then  the tempo training line should show a step of 3 bpm

  @ft:19
  Scenario: Decrease the tempo-training step size
    Given the tempo-training step is 2 BPM
    When  I press "["
    Then  the tempo training line should show a step of 1 bpm

  @ft:20
  Scenario: Tempo-training step size cannot go below the minimum
    Given the tempo-training step is 1 BPM
    When  I press "["
    Then  the tempo training line should show a step of 1 bpm

  @ft:21
  Scenario: Tempo-training step size cannot go above the maximum
    Given the tempo-training step is 20 BPM
    When  I press "]"
    Then  the tempo training line should show a step of 20 bpm

  @ft:22
  Scenario: Adjusting the step size works while the metronome is stopped
    Given the metronome is stopped
    And   the tempo-training step is 2 BPM
    When  I press "]"
    Then  the tempo training line should show a step of 3 bpm

  @ft:23
  Scenario: Changed step size is used on the next tempo-training increase
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  I press "]"
    And   8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 131 BPM"

  @ft:24
  Scenario: Increase the tempo-training interval
    Given the tempo-training interval is 8 measures
    When  I press "}"
    Then  the tempo training line should show an interval of 9 measures

  @ft:25
  Scenario: Decrease the tempo-training interval
    Given the tempo-training interval is 8 measures
    When  I press "{"
    Then  the tempo training line should show an interval of 7 measures

  @ft:26
  Scenario: Tempo-training interval cannot go below the minimum
    Given the tempo-training interval is 1 measure
    When  I press "{"
    Then  the tempo training line should show an interval of 1 measure

  @ft:27
  Scenario: Tempo-training interval cannot go above the maximum
    Given the tempo-training interval is 32 measures
    When  I press "}"
    Then  the tempo training line should show an interval of 32 measures

  @ft:28
  Scenario: Adjusting the interval works while the metronome is stopped
    Given the metronome is stopped
    And   the tempo-training interval is 8 measures
    When  I press "}"
    Then  the tempo training line should show an interval of 9 measures

  @ft:29
  Scenario: Changed interval is used for the next tempo-training increase
    Given tempo training is enabled with step 10 BPM every 8 measures
    And   the BPM is 120
    And   the metronome is playing
    When  I press "}"
    And   8 measures have elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should still show "♩ = 120 BPM"
    When  1 more measure has elapsed
    Then  the BPM readout should show "♩ = 130 BPM"
